{"reasoning":"pakad: The signature descending phrase 'd n P m P g m R S' appears verbatim in the taan and is thoroughly integrated into the mukhada via '(P)d~ n P P m P P g<>m g<>m R S'. The purvanga half 'S R g R g m P' is not explicitly quoted in full, but its essence is consistently evoked through '(R)g~ m P'. Score: 4.

idiom: The line demonstrates deep Darbari grammar: 25% mandra residency with 62% lower-tetrachord weight honours the raga's grave centre of gravity. komal ga and komal dha are consistently treated with canonical kan and andolan ('(R)g~', '(m)g~', '(P)d~', '(n)d~'), and descent avoids plain linear n-d-P in favour of vakra turns like 'd n P'. The gamak oscillations ('g<>m') in the mukhada and manjha provide genuine weight. Score: 4.

rasa: The sombre, meditative, late-night majesty of Darbari is sustained powerfully, aided by the unhurried dwell times in the mandra octave and deliberate oscillation on g and d. It captures the heavy gambhir mood demanded by both the raga and the doom aesthetic without turning into scalar speed exercises. Score: 4.","scores":{"pakad":4,"idiom":4,"rasa":4},"notes":"The lead captures Darbari's heavy, nocturnal character with proper andolan on ga and dha, and grounds the bulk of its movement in the mandra and lower madhya saptaks. To elevate authenticity further, explicitly state the opening half of the pakad (S R g R g m P) in the intro alap, and ensure the final cadence settles on madhya Sa rather than dropping abruptly to the lower octave.","suggestions":[{"section":0,"change":"Replace 'S[1] R[1.5] g~[3.5] m[1] g~[3] m[1.5] P[1]' with 'S[1] R[1.5] (R)g~[2] R[1] (R)g~[1.5] m[1] P[3]'","why":"Establishes the quintessential purvanga pakad motif (S R g R g m P) with the signature oscillation and turn on komal ga early in the alap."},{"section":8,"change":"Replace the final '(R)g~[1] m[1] R[1] S(-1)[9]' with '(R)g~[1] m[1] R[2] S[8]'","why":"In Darbari, concluding cadences settle with dignity on vadi R before dying away on home madhya Sa, rather than dropping an octave down to S(-1)."}]}
